const enBody = `<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">${enTitle}</h1>

<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4"><strong>Firecrawl</strong> (firecrawl.dev) is a Y Combinator W23 startup whose entire product is one API for turning the live web into clean LLM-ready data. Where BeautifulSoup and Cheerio break on every JS-rendered SPA, login-walled page, and bot-detection trigger, Firecrawl ships <strong>nine v2 endpoints</strong> behind one credit system and one API key: <strong>Scrape</strong> for single-page markdown / HTML / JSON conversion, <strong>Crawl</strong> for recursive whole-site walks, <strong>Map</strong> for URL discovery, <strong>Search</strong> for web search + scrape fusion, <strong>Batch Scrape</strong> for explicit URL lists, <strong>Extract</strong> for LLM-driven structured extraction across many URLs, <strong>Interact</strong> for Playwright code or natural-language browser automation, <strong>Monitor</strong> for scheduled diff tracking, and <strong>Agent</strong> for autonomous multi-site research. For an engineer building a web-aware agent in August 2026, Firecrawl matters because it collapses the scrape + parse + extract pipeline into one HTTP call and exposes the whole stack as an MCP server that Claude Code / Cursor / Windsurf can drive directly. See the full <a href="/providers/firecrawl">Firecrawl provider page</a> for the structured comparison table.</p>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-lg p-4 my-4"><strong>🌍 Quick take:</strong> Firecrawl is the first web-scraping API designed for in-agent invocation. The v2 JSON mode collapses the two-step "scrape then LLM extract" workflow into one call by embedding an OpenAI-format schema directly in the <code>formats</code> array. maxAge page cache defaults to 2 days for millisecond returns on cache hits. The self-hosted AGPL-3.0 Docker / Kubernetes build gives enterprises a clean path around mainland-China latency and compliance. Free tier with no credit card: 1,000 credits/month + 5 daily Agent runs. No mainland China hosted endpoint.</div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">What Firecrawl is, and why its API matters in 2026</h2>

<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">Firecrawl is the public API of <strong>Firecrawl, Inc.</strong>, a Y Combinator W23 startup whose founding premise is that every web-aware AI agent eventually needs the same scraping pipeline and that pipeline should not be rebuilt per project. Where OpenAI's <a href="/tutorials/openai-gpt-red-api-security-2026">GPT API</a> and Anthropic's <a href="/tutorials/anthropic-claude-api-review">Claude API</a> optimize for general chat reasoning and Fireworks / Together / DeepInfra optimize for LLM inference cost, Firecrawl optimizes for the four operations a web agent does on every turn:</p>

<ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-gray-700 space-y-2 my-4">
<li><strong>Scrape</strong> a single URL — convert HTML to markdown, JSON, or structured data (JSON mode).</li>
<li><strong>Crawl</strong> an entire website — recursively walk from a starting URL to the configured depth.</li>
<li><strong>Search</strong> the web — search-engine-style query that optionally scrapes the top results in the same call.</li>
<li><strong>Monitor</strong> a URL / website / web-scale search — schedule recurring checks and notify on diff.</li>
</ol>

<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">Behind those four primary operations sit five complementary endpoints. <strong>Map</strong> lists every URL on a website without scraping content (useful for sitemap discovery and crawl planning). <strong>Batch Scrape</strong> accepts an explicit URL list and returns all results in one concurrent job (sync + async modes). <strong>Extract</strong> is the LLM-driven structured-extraction endpoint for many URLs / URL patterns — the batch sibling of the single-URL JSON mode. <strong>Interact</strong> provides a browser sandbox for Playwright code or natural-language prompts — login-walled pages, JS-rendered SPAs, form fills, end-to-end web tests. <strong>Agent</strong> runs autonomous research across multiple sites, optionally returning a JSON schema; 5 daily runs are free on every plan.</p>

<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">The other reason Firecrawl keeps showing up in 2026 agent builds: the v2 <strong>JSON mode</strong> collapses the canonical two-step scrape-extract pipeline into one call. The v1 API had a separate <code>jsonOptions</code> parameter that lived outside the formats array; the v2 API removed it and lets you embed an OpenAI-format schema directly in <code is:raw>ts: [{`{type: "json", schema: {...}}`}]</code>. The response returns <code is:raw>{`{success: true, data: {...}}`}</code> with <code>data</code> already conforming to the schema — no second LLM call, no second parsing layer, no schema mapping glue code.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">The Firecrawl v2 product lineup</h2>

<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-4">Firecrawl ships nine v2 endpoints, each with a clearly bounded use case. The headline matrix:</p>

<table class="table-token min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 my-4">
<thead>
